## Tagged by dgt5v

## DBsubject(Statistics)
## DBchapter(Sample survey methods)
## DBsection(Concepts)
## Institution(ASU)
## MLT(IDSamplingMethod)
## MLTleader(1)
## Level(2)
## KEYWORDS('Statistics','Sampling')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserRadioButtons.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Numeric');

$radio = RadioButtons(
    [ [
        'Multistage Sample',
        'Stratified Random Sample',
        'Systematic Random Sample',
        'Cluster Sample',
        'Simple Random Sample'
    ] ],
    0,
    labels => 'ABC'
);

BEGIN_PGML

To select students at ASU to complete a survey, 10 schedule line numbers are selected at random from the class schedule.  Then 5 students in each selected class are randomly selected to complete the survey.  What type of sample is this?

[_]{$radio}
END_PGML
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Because there are two stages of randomly selecting samples, this is a *Multistage Sample* or [$radio].
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();        # This should be the last executable line in the problem.